-- title:
--   Integrality over ℂ[̄ j] bounds analytic orders on H
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be a finite-index subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ containing the translation matrix $T$, let $k$ be an integer, let $m$ be a natural number with $m \ge 1$, and let $g,h$ be modular forms of weight $k$ for the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$. Let $X \in \mathbb{C}((q))$ be a Laurent series such that $X$ times the $q$-expansion of $h$ of period $1$ equals the $q$-expansion of $g$ of period $1$, both expansions being viewed as Laurent series via the inclusion of $\mathbb{C}[[q]]$. Write $\bar j =$ [`ModularCurve.jqModC ℂ`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15) for the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the image in $\mathbb{C}[[q]]$ of the integral power series $\mathrm{eisenstein4}^3 \cdot \mathrm{dedekindEtaUnitInv}$, i.e. the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$. Assume that $X^6 \cdot \bar j^{\,4m} \cdot (\bar j - 1728)^{3m}$ is integral over the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of $\mathbb{C}((q))$ generated by $\bar j$. Then for every $\tau$ in the upper half-plane, the analytic order of vanishing at the point $\tau \in \mathbb{C}$ of the function $z \mapsto h(z)\,\Delta(z)^m$, transported to $\mathbb{C}$ by precomposition with `UpperHalfPlane.ofComplex`, is at most the analytic order of vanishing at $\tau$ of $z \mapsto g(z)\,(E_4(z)^2 E_6(z))^m$, transported in the same way.
--
--   This is the local form, at points of the upper half-plane, of the standard passage from an integral dependence relation over $\mathbb{C}[j]$ to an inequality of divisors: the monic relation, read on $\mathbb{H}$, bounds below the order of $g\,(E_4^2E_6)^m/(h\,\Delta^m)$ at the zeros of $E_4$ and $E_6$. It is used in the construction of modular and cusp forms with prescribed $q$-expansion, being cited by [`ModularCurve.exists_cuspForm_qExpansion_eq_mul_thetaL_pow_of_isIntegral_qExpFunctionFieldC`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_cuspForm_qExpansion_eq_mul_thetaL_pow_of_isIntegral_qExpFunctionFieldC) and [`ModularCurve.exists_modularForm_gamma1_qExpansion_eq_mul_thetaL_pow_of_isIntegral`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_modularForm_gamma1_qExpansion_eq_mul_thetaL_pow_of_isIntegral).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_analyticOrderAt_le_of_isIntegral_adjoin_jqModC_pow.lean

import Mathlib
